      "title": "STUN: Use message length in version heuristics",
      "message": "STUN: Use message length in version heuristics\n\nIf the STUN version is set to autodetect, and the message length\nis not a multiple of 4 bytes (as it must be in RFC 5389, where\npadding the attribute lengths was introduced), then dissect it\nas the earlier version instead of adding an expert info (and\nalso throwing an exception later most likely by rounding up.)\n",
